-- title:
--   Height drops by one modulo an element avoiding minimal primes
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative Noetherian ring, let $p \subseteq R$ be a prime ideal, and let $x \in R$ be an element with $x \in p$ such that for every $q$ in $\mathrm{minimalPrimes}\ R$ with $q \le p$ one has $x \notin q$; that is, $x$ lies in no minimal prime of $R$ contained in $p$. Write $J = (x)$ for the ideal generated by $x$ and let $p \cdot (R/J)$ denote the image $p.\mathrm{map}(\mathrm{Ideal.Quotient.mk}\ J)$ of $p$ under the quotient map $R \to R/(x)$. The conclusion is the identity of heights (as elements of $\mathbb{N}\cup\{\infty\}$ with $\mathrm{Ideal.height}$)
--   $$\operatorname{ht}\bigl(p\,(R/(x))\bigr) + 1 = \operatorname{ht}(p),$$
--   so that passing to $R/(x)$ lowers the height of $p$ by exactly one. Note that the conclusion is stated as an equation about the image ideal itself, with no separate hypothesis that this image is prime; primality of the image is derived inside the proof from $(x) \le p$.
--
--   This is the standard statement that cutting by an element of a prime $p$ which avoids all minimal primes below $p$ drops the height of $p$ by exactly one, the local-algebra input to inductive arguments on dimension. It is used in the induction establishing the dimension formula for Cohen–Macaulay local rings, via [`IsLocalRing.IsCohenMacaulayOfDim.ringKrullDim_quotient_add_height`](thm.html#IsLocalRing.IsCohenMacaulayOfDim.ringKrullDim_quotient_add_height).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Ideal_height_map_quotientMk_span_singleton_add_one.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

theorem Ideal.height_map_quotientMk_span_singleton_add_one
    {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R] (p : Ideal R) [p.IsPrime] {x : R} (hx : x ∈ p)
    (hxmin : ∀ q ∈ minimalPrimes R, q ≤ p → x ∉ q) :
    (p.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span {x}))).height + 1 = p.height := by sorry
